IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa5-loans-exceptions.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 10, Chapter 4 (transactions requiring members' approval), the part of the
-- Chapter that lies in coa5's ranges: ss 205 to 214 (lines 2697-2821 of ukpga-2006-46.txt): the exceptions to the approval
-- requirements for loans etc (ss 205 to 209), what counts as "other relevant transactions" (s 210), the value of a transaction
-- (s 211), the person for whom it is entered into (s 212), the civil consequences of contravention (s 213) and affirmation (s 214).
-- Ss 197 to 203 (the requirements themselves) belong to coa4: their answers come in as INPUTS named for the section (see NOTES.md, Seams).
--
-- SOURCE: a plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; not the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer). A decision function answers MAYBE BOOLEAN.
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words (a "means" definition, an "if", "unless", "where" or period it states,
--               a closed list, a flat negative). Each such branch carries  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<words>"
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide (lists without closing, "includes", silent, points outside the text, a grant or bar
--               limited by its own wording and the case falls outside the limit). Each such branch carries  -- NOTHING-kind (<why>)
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- An exception that says "approval is not required ... if ..." is encoded as the question "is approval removed by THIS section":
-- JUST TRUE when its conditions are met, JUST FALSE when an "if" it states is not met (reading (a), for a lawyer), NOTHING when
-- the case is outside the kind of thing it speaks of. JUST FALSE never says that approval IS required: it says only that this
-- section does not remove the requirement on these facts.

§ `Chapter 4 (ss 205 to 214): exceptions, relevant transactions, value, consequences`

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 205 Exception for expenditure on defending proceedings etc
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- src lines for the whole of s 205(5)
-- src:2719 | (5) The reference in subsection (1)(a)(ii) to an application for relief is to an application for relief under—
-- src:2720 | section 661(3) or (4) (power of court to grant relief in case of acquisition of shares by innocent nominee), or
-- src:2721 | section 1157 (general power of court to grant relief in case of honest and reasonable conduct).
@ref s 205(5) application for relief (src:2719-2721)
DECLARE `s 205(5) provision for relief` IS ONE OF
    `s 205(5) section 661(3) or (4)`
    `s 205(5) section 1157`
    `s 205(5) some other provision`

-- src:2719 | (5) The reference in subsection (1)(a)(ii) to an application for relief is to an application for relief under—
-- src:2720 | section 661(3) or (4) (power of court to grant relief in case of acquisition of shares by innocent nominee), or
-- src:2721 | section 1157 (general power of court to grant relief in case of honest and reasonable conduct).
@ref s 205(5) application for relief (src:2719-2721)
GIVEN provision IS A `s 205(5) provision for relief`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205(5) the application is an application for relief` MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `s 205(5) section 661(3) or (4)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 205(5) section 1157` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 205(5) some other provision` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is to an application for relief under— section 661(3) or (4) ... or section 1157"

-- src:2713 | (3) For this purpose a conviction, judgment or refusal of relief becomes final—
-- src:2714 | (a) if not appealed against, at the end of the period for bringing an appeal;
-- src:2715 | (b) if appealed against, when the appeal (or any further appeal) is disposed of.
@ref s 205(3) when a conviction, judgment or refusal of relief becomes final (src:2713-2715)
GIVEN `the conviction, judgment or refusal of relief is appealed against` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date when the period for bringing an appeal ends` IS A DATE
      `the date when the appeal (or any further appeal) is disposed of` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 205(3) the date when the conviction, judgment or refusal of relief becomes final` MEANS
    IF `the conviction, judgment or refusal of relief is appealed against`
    THEN `the date when the appeal (or any further appeal) is disposed of` -- (b) if appealed against, when the appeal (or any further appeal) is disposed of
    ELSE `the date when the period for bringing an appeal ends` -- (a) if not appealed against, at the end of the period for bringing an appeal

-- src:2716 | (4) An appeal is disposed of—
-- src:2717 | (a) if it is determined and the period for bringing any further appeal has ended, or
-- src:2718 | (b) if it is abandoned or otherwise ceases to have effect.
@ref s 205(4) when an appeal is disposed of (src:2716-2718)
GIVEN determined IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period for bringing any further appeal has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `abandoned or otherwise ceased to have effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205(4) the appeal is disposed of` MEANS
    IF (determined AND `the period for bringing any further appeal has ended`) OR `abandoned or otherwise ceased to have effect`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An appeal is disposed of— (a) if it is determined and the period for bringing any further appeal has ended, or (b) if it is abandoned or otherwise ceases to have effect"

-- Pass the facts for whichever of the three events the proceedings can end in: conviction (criminal proceedings), judgment
-- against the director (civil proceedings) or refusal of relief (an application for relief). The text does not say which events
-- a loan's terms must cover (fork F-205-1 in NOTES.md).
-- src:2704 | (2) The terms are—
-- src:2705 | (a) that the loan is to be repaid, or (as the case may be) any liability of the company incurred under any transaction connected with the thing done is to be discharged, in the event of—
-- src:2706 | (i) the director being convicted in the proceedings,
-- src:2707 | (ii) judgment being given against him in the proceedings, or
-- src:2708 | (iii) the court refusing to grant him relief on the application; and
-- src:2709 | (b) that it is to be so repaid or discharged not later than—
-- src:2710 | (i) the date when the conviction becomes final,
-- src:2711 | (ii) the date when the judgment becomes final, or
-- src:2712 | (iii) the date when the refusal of relief becomes final.
@ref s 205(2) the terms (src:2704-2712)
GIVEN `the terms require repayment or discharge in the event` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the latest date the terms allow for repayment or discharge` IS A DATE
      `the date when the conviction, judgment or refusal of relief becomes final` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205(2) the terms are met` MEANS
    IF `the terms require repayment or discharge in the event`
       AND `the latest date the terms allow for repayment or discharge` AT MOST `the date when the conviction, judgment or refusal of relief becomes final`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The terms are— (a) that the loan is to be repaid ... and (b) that it is to be so repaid or discharged not later than"

DECLARE `s 205(1) what the company does` IS ONE OF
    `s 205(1)(a)(i) provides funds to meet expenditure in defending criminal or civil proceedings`
    `s 205(1)(a)(ii) provides funds to meet expenditure in connection with an application for relief` HAS `s 205(1)(a)(ii) provision under which relief is sought` IS A `s 205(5) provision for relief`
    `s 205(1)(b) enables the director to avoid incurring such expenditure`
    `s 205(1) does something else`

-- src:2698 | (1) Approval is not required under section 197, 198, 200 or 201 (requirement of members' approval for loans etc) for anything done by a company—
-- src:2699 | (a) to provide a director of the company or of its holding company with funds to meet expenditure incurred or to be incurred by him—
-- src:2700 | (i) in defending any criminal or civil proceedings in connection with any alleged negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust by him in relation to the company or an associated company, or
-- src:2701 | (ii) in connection with an application for relief (see subsection (5)), or
-- src:2702 | (b) to enable any such director to avoid incurring such expenditure,
-- src:2703 | if it is done on the following terms.
@ref s 205(1) exception for expenditure on defending proceedings (src:2698-2703)
GIVEN `what the company does` IS A `s 205(1) what the company does`
      `the person is a director of the company or of its holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings concern alleged negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust by him in relation to the company or an associated company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms in subsection (2) are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 205(1) approval under sections 197, 198, 200 and 201 is not required by this section` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is a director of the company or of its holding company`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a director of the company or of its holding company"
    ELSE CONSIDER `what the company does`
         WHEN `s 205(1)(a)(i) provides funds to meet expenditure in defending criminal or civil proceedings` THEN
              IF `the proceedings concern alleged negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust by him in relation to the company or an associated company`
              THEN IF `the terms in subsection (2) are met`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is done on the following terms"
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in connection with any alleged negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust by him in relation to the company or an associated company"
         WHEN `s 205(1)(a)(ii) provides funds to meet expenditure in connection with an application for relief` relief THEN
              CONSIDER `s 205(5) the application is an application for relief` relief
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
                   IF `the terms in subsection (2) are met`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is done on the following terms"
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in connection with an application for relief (see subsection (5))"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent)
         WHEN `s 205(1)(b) enables the director to avoid incurring such expenditure` THEN
              IF `the proceedings concern alleged negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust by him in relation to the company or an associated company`
              THEN IF `the terms in subsection (2) are met`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is done on the following terms"
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to enable any such director to avoid incurring such expenditure"
         WHEN `s 205(1) does something else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for anything done by a company— (a) to provide a director ... or (b) to enable any such director to avoid"

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 206 Exception for expenditure in connection with regulatory action or investigation
-- ======================================================================================================================

DECLARE `s 206 what the company does` IS ONE OF
    `s 206(a)(i) provides funds to meet expenditure in defending himself in an investigation by a regulatory authority`
    `s 206(a)(ii) provides funds to meet expenditure in defending himself against action proposed to be taken by a regulatory authority`
    `s 206(b) enables the director to avoid incurring such expenditure`
    `s 206 does something else`

-- src:2723 | Approval is not required under section 197, 198, 200 or 201 (requirement of members' approval for loans etc) for anything done by a company—
-- src:2724 | (a) to provide a director of the company or of its holding company with funds to meet expenditure incurred or to be incurred by him in defending himself—
-- src:2725 | (i) in an investigation by a regulatory authority, or
-- src:2726 | (ii) against action proposed to be taken by a regulatory authority,
-- src:2727 | in connection with any alleged negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust by him in relation to the company or an associated company, or
-- src:2728 | (b) to enable any such director to avoid incurring such expenditure.
@ref s 206 exception for expenditure in connection with regulatory action or investigation (src:2723-2728)
GIVEN `what the company does` IS A `s 206 what the company does`
      `the person is a director of the company or of its holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is in connection with alleged negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust by him in relation to the company or an associated company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 206 approval under sections 197, 198, 200 and 201 is not required by this section` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is a director of the company or of its holding company`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a director of the company or of its holding company"
        IF NOT `the matter is in connection with alleged negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust by him in relation to the company or an associated company`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in connection with any alleged negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust by him in relation to the company or an associated company"
        IF `what the company does` EQUALS `s 206 does something else`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for anything done by a company— (a) to provide a director ... (b) to enable any such director to avoid incurring such expenditure"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 207 Exceptions for minor and business transactions
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- The value of a transaction (s 211): a specific sum of pounds, or, where the value cannot be expressed as a specific sum,
-- deemed to exceed 50,000 pounds (s 211(7)).
DECLARE `s 211 value` IS ONE OF
    `s 211 a specific sum` HAS `s 211 pounds` IS A NUMBER
    `s 211 deemed to exceed 50000 pounds`

-- A value deemed to exceed 50,000 pounds exceeds any sum not above 50,000; whether it exceeds a larger sum the text does not say.
-- src:2786 | (7) If the value of a transaction or arrangement is not capable of being expressed as a specific sum of money—
-- src:2787 | (a) whether because the amount of any liability arising under the transaction or arrangement is unascertainable, or for any other reason, and
-- src:2788 | (b) whether or not any liability under the transaction or arrangement has been reduced,
-- src:2789 | its value is deemed to exceed £50,000.
@ref s 211(7) deemed value (src:2786-2789)
GIVEN a IS A `s 211 value`, b IS A `s 211 value`, limit IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 211(7) the aggregate of the two values exceeds the sum` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (a EQUALS `s 211 deemed to exceed 50000 pounds` OR b EQUALS `s 211 deemed to exceed 50000 pounds`) AND limit AT MOST 50_000
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF a EQUALS `s 211 deemed to exceed 50000 pounds` OR b EQUALS `s 211 deemed to exceed 50000 pounds`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a value deemed to exceed 50,000 pounds is not known to exceed a larger sum
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the pounds of` a PLUS `the pounds of` b GREATER THAN limit)
    WHERE
        `the pounds of` v MEANS
            CONSIDER v
            WHEN `s 211 a specific sum` x THEN x
            WHEN `s 211 deemed to exceed 50000 pounds` THEN 0 -- not reached: both values are specific sums on this branch

-- src:2730 | (1) Approval is not required under section 197, 198 or 200 for a company to make a loan or quasi-loan, or to give a guarantee or provide security in connection with a loan or quasi-loan, if the aggregate of—
-- src:2731 | (a) the value of the transaction, and
-- src:2732 | (b) the value of any other relevant transactions or arrangements,
-- src:2733 | does not exceed £10,000.
@ref s 207(1) the sum (src:2730-2733)
`s 207(1) the sum in pounds` MEANS 10_000

-- src:2734 | (2) Approval is not required under section 201 for a company to enter into a credit transaction, or to give a guarantee or provide security in connection with a credit transaction, if the aggregate of—
-- src:2735 | (a) the value of the transaction (that is, of the credit transaction, guarantee or security), and
-- src:2736 | (b) the value of any other relevant transactions or arrangements,
-- src:2737 | does not exceed £15,000.
@ref s 207(2) the sum (src:2734-2737)
`s 207(2) the sum in pounds` MEANS 15_000

DECLARE `s 207 transaction` IS ONE OF
    `s 207 a loan`
    `s 207 a quasi-loan`
    `s 207 a guarantee or security in connection with a loan or quasi-loan`
    `s 207 a credit transaction`
    `s 207 a guarantee or security in connection with a credit transaction`
    `s 207 another kind of transaction`

-- src:2730 | (1) Approval is not required under section 197, 198 or 200 for a company to make a loan or quasi-loan, or to give a guarantee or provide security in connection with a loan or quasi-loan, if the aggregate of—
-- src:2731 | (a) the value of the transaction, and
-- src:2732 | (b) the value of any other relevant transactions or arrangements,
-- src:2733 | does not exceed £10,000.
@ref s 207(1) minor loans (src:2730-2733)
GIVEN transaction IS A `s 207 transaction`
      `the value of the transaction` IS A `s 211 value`
      `the value of any other relevant transactions or arrangements` IS A `s 211 value`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(1) approval under sections 197, 198 and 200 is not required by this section` MEANS
    CONSIDER transaction
    WHEN `s 207 a loan` THEN `s 207(1) the aggregate test`
    WHEN `s 207 a quasi-loan` THEN `s 207(1) the aggregate test`
    WHEN `s 207 a guarantee or security in connection with a loan or quasi-loan` THEN `s 207(1) the aggregate test`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to make a loan or quasi-loan, or to give a guarantee or provide security in connection with a loan or quasi-loan"
    WHERE
        `s 207(1) the aggregate test` MEANS
            IF `s 211(7) the aggregate of the two values exceeds the sum` `the value of the transaction` `the value of any other relevant transactions or arrangements` (`s 207(1) the sum in pounds`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the aggregate of— (a) the value of the transaction, and (b) the value of any other relevant transactions or arrangements, does not exceed £10,000"
            ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:2734 | (2) Approval is not required under section 201 for a company to enter into a credit transaction, or to give a guarantee or provide security in connection with a credit transaction, if the aggregate of—
-- src:2735 | (a) the value of the transaction (that is, of the credit transaction, guarantee or security), and
-- src:2736 | (b) the value of any other relevant transactions or arrangements,
-- src:2737 | does not exceed £15,000.
@ref s 207(2) minor credit transactions (src:2734-2737)
GIVEN transaction IS A `s 207 transaction`
      `the value of the transaction` IS A `s 211 value`
      `the value of any other relevant transactions or arrangements` IS A `s 211 value`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(2) approval under section 201 is not required by this section` MEANS
    CONSIDER transaction
    WHEN `s 207 a credit transaction` THEN `s 207(2) the aggregate test`
    WHEN `s 207 a guarantee or security in connection with a credit transaction` THEN `s 207(2) the aggregate test`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to enter into a credit transaction, or to give a guarantee or provide security in connection with a credit transaction"
    WHERE
        `s 207(2) the aggregate test` MEANS
            IF `s 211(7) the aggregate of the two values exceeds the sum` `the value of the transaction` `the value of any other relevant transactions or arrangements` (`s 207(2) the sum in pounds`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the aggregate of— (a) the value of the transaction (that is, of the credit transaction, guarantee or security), and (b) the value of any other relevant transactions or arrangements, does not exceed £15,000"
            ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:2738 | (3) Approval is not required under section 201 for a company to enter into a credit transaction, or to give a guarantee or provide security in connection with a credit transaction, if—
-- src:2739 | (a) the transaction is entered into by the company in the ordinary course of the company's business, and
-- src:2740 | (b) the value of the transaction is not greater, and the terms on which it is entered into are not more favourable, than it is reasonable to expect the company would have offered to, or in respect of, a person of the same financial standing but unconnected with the company.
@ref s 207(3) credit transactions in the ordinary course of business (src:2738-2740)
GIVEN transaction IS A `s 207 transaction`
      `entered into by the company in the ordinary course of the company's business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value is not greater than it is reasonable to expect the company would have offered to an unconnected person of the same financial standing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms are not more favourable than it is reasonable to expect the company would have offered to an unconnected person of the same financial standing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 207(3) approval under section 201 is not required by this section` MEANS
    CONSIDER transaction
    WHEN `s 207 a credit transaction` THEN `s 207(3) the conditions`
    WHEN `s 207 a guarantee or security in connection with a credit transaction` THEN `s 207(3) the conditions`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to enter into a credit transaction, or to give a guarantee or provide security in connection with a credit transaction"
    WHERE
        `s 207(3) the conditions` MEANS
            IF     `entered into by the company in the ordinary course of the company's business`
               AND `the value is not greater than it is reasonable to expect the company would have offered to an unconnected person of the same financial standing`
               AND `the terms are not more favourable than it is reasonable to expect the company would have offered to an unconnected person of the same financial standing`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if— (a) the transaction is entered into by the company in the ordinary course of the company's business, and (b) the value of the transaction is not greater, and the terms ... are not more favourable"

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 208 Exceptions for intra-group transactions
-- ======================================================================================================================

DECLARE `s 208 transaction` IS ONE OF
    `s 208(1)(a) the making of a loan or quasi-loan to the other body corporate`
    `s 208(1)(b) a guarantee or security in connection with a loan or quasi-loan made to the other body corporate`
    `s 208(2)(a) a credit transaction entered into as creditor for the benefit of the other body corporate`
    `s 208(2)(b) a guarantee or security in connection with a credit transaction entered into by any person for the benefit of the other body corporate`
    `s 208 another kind of transaction`

-- `s 256(a) the bodies corporate are associated` is the answer of s 256(a) below (this part).
-- src:2742 | (1) Approval is not required under section 197, 198 or 200 for—
-- src:2743 | (a) the making of a loan or quasi-loan to an associated body corporate, or
-- src:2744 | (b) the giving of a guarantee or provision of security in connection with a loan or quasi-loan made to an associated body corporate.
-- src:2745 | (2) Approval is not required under section 201—
-- src:2746 | (a) to enter into a credit transaction as creditor for the benefit of an associated body corporate, or
-- src:2747 | (b) to give a guarantee or provide security in connection with a credit transaction entered into by any person for the benefit of an associated body corporate.
@ref s 208 exceptions for intra-group transactions (src:2742-2747)
GIVEN transaction IS A `s 208 transaction`
      `s 256(a) the bodies corporate are associated` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 208 approval is not required by this section` MEANS
    CONSIDER transaction
    WHEN `s 208 another kind of transaction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for— (a) the making of a loan or quasi-loan to an associated body corporate, or (b) the giving of a guarantee"
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `s 256(a) the bodies corporate are associated`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to an associated body corporate" (the text exempts dealings with an associated body corporate and says nothing of any other)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the bodies are associated turns on s 1159 (subsidiary), asked in s 256

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 209 Exceptions for money-lending companies
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- src:2752 | (2) A “money-lending company” means a company whose ordinary business includes the making of loans or quasi-loans, or the giving of guarantees or provision of security in connection with loans or quasi-loans.
@ref s 209(2) money-lending company (src:2752)
GIVEN `the company's ordinary business includes the making of loans or quasi-loans` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's ordinary business includes giving guarantees or providing security in connection with loans or quasi-loans` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 209(2) the company is a money-lending company` MEANS
    IF `the company's ordinary business includes the making of loans or quasi-loans` OR `the company's ordinary business includes giving guarantees or providing security in connection with loans or quasi-loans`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A “money-lending company” means a company whose ordinary business includes"

DECLARE `s 209(4) purpose of a loan` IS ONE OF
    `s 209(4)(a) purchase of the whole or part of a dwelling-house, with land to be occupied and enjoyed with it`
    `s 209(4)(b) improving a dwelling-house or part of one so used, or land occupied and enjoyed with it`
    `s 209(4)(c) substitution for a loan made by any person and falling within paragraph (a) or (b)`
    `s 209(4) some other purpose`

-- src:2757 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (3) a “home loan” means a loan—
-- src:2758 | (a) for the purpose of facilitating the purchase, for use as the only or main residence of the person to whom the loan is made, of the whole or part of any dwelling-house together with any land to be occupied and enjoyed with it,
-- src:2759 | (b) for the purpose of improving a dwelling-house or part of a dwelling-house so used or any land occupied and enjoyed with it, or
-- src:2760 | (c) in substitution for any loan made by any person and falling within paragraph (a) or (b).
@ref s 209(4) home loan (src:2757-2760)
GIVEN purpose IS A `s 209(4) purpose of a loan`
      `the dwelling-house is for use as the only or main residence of the person to whom the loan is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 209(4) the loan is a home loan` MEANS
    CONSIDER purpose
    WHEN `s 209(4)(a) purchase of the whole or part of a dwelling-house, with land to be occupied and enjoyed with it` THEN
         IF `the dwelling-house is for use as the only or main residence of the person to whom the loan is made`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a “home loan” means a loan— (a) for the purpose of facilitating the purchase, for use as the only or main residence of the person to whom the loan is made"
    WHEN `s 209(4)(b) improving a dwelling-house or part of one so used, or land occupied and enjoyed with it` THEN
         IF `the dwelling-house is for use as the only or main residence of the person to whom the loan is made`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a “home loan” means a loan— ... (b) for the purpose of improving a dwelling-house or part of a dwelling-house so used"
    WHEN `s 209(4)(c) substitution for a loan made by any person and falling within paragraph (a) or (b)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 209(4) some other purpose` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“home loan” means a loan— (a) ... (b) ... or (c) ..."

DECLARE `s 209(3) borrower` IS ONE OF
    `s 209(3)(a) a director of the company or of its holding company`
    `s 209(3)(b) an employee of the company`
    `s 209(3) someone else`

-- src:2753 | (3) The condition specified in subsection (1)(b) does not of itself prevent a company from making a home loan—
-- src:2754 | (a) to a director of the company or of its holding company, or
-- src:2755 | (b) to an employee of the company,
-- src:2756 | if loans of that description are ordinarily made by the company to its employees and the terms of the loan in question are no more favourable than those on which such loans are ordinarily made.
@ref s 209(3) home loans (src:2753-2756)
GIVEN borrower IS A `s 209(3) borrower`
      `the loan is a home loan` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `loans of that description are ordinarily made by the company to its employees` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms are no more favourable than those on which such loans are ordinarily made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 209(3) the condition in subsection (1)(b) does not of itself prevent the company from making the home loan` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the loan is a home loan`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "from making a home loan"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent)
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
         CONSIDER borrower
         WHEN `s 209(3) someone else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) to a director of the company or of its holding company, or (b) to an employee of the company"
         OTHERWISE
              IF `loans of that description are ordinarily made by the company to its employees` AND `the terms are no more favourable than those on which such loans are ordinarily made`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if loans of that description are ordinarily made by the company to its employees and the terms of the loan in question are no more favourable than those on which such loans are ordinarily made"

-- src:2749 | (1) Approval is not required under section 197, 198 or 200 for the making of a loan or quasi-loan, or the giving of a guarantee or provision of security in connection with a loan or quasi-loan, by a money-lending company if—
-- src:2750 | (a) the transaction (that is, the loan, quasi-loan, guarantee or security) is entered into by the company in the ordinary course of the company's business, and
-- src:2751 | (b) the value of the transaction is not greater, and its terms are not more favourable, than it is reasonable to expect the company would have offered to a person of the same financial standing but unconnected with the company.
@ref s 209(1) money-lending companies (src:2749-2751)
GIVEN transaction IS A `s 207 transaction`
      `the company is a money-lending company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `entered into by the company in the ordinary course of the company's business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value is not greater, and the terms are not more favourable, than it is reasonable to expect the company would have offered to an unconnected person of the same financial standing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition in subsection (1)(b) does not of itself prevent a home loan` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 209(1) approval under sections 197, 198 and 200 is not required by this section` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF    transaction EQUALS `s 207 a credit transaction`
           OR transaction EQUALS `s 207 a guarantee or security in connection with a credit transaction`
           OR transaction EQUALS `s 207 another kind of transaction`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the making of a loan or quasi-loan, or the giving of a guarantee or provision of security in connection with a loan or quasi-loan"
        IF `the company is a money-lending company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by a money-lending company"
        IF `the company is a money-lending company` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the company is a money-lending company is not known
        IF NOT `entered into by the company in the ordinary course of the company's business`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if— (a) the transaction ... is entered into by the company in the ordinary course of the company's business"
        IF `the value is not greater, and the terms are not more favourable, than it is reasonable to expect the company would have offered to an unconnected person of the same financial standing`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the condition in subsection (1)(b) does not of itself prevent a home loan` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE -- s 209(3): the condition in (1)(b) does not of itself prevent a home loan to a director or an employee
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- s 209(3) answering NOTHING (it speaks only of a home loan to a director or an employee) is read as "does not rescue the transaction" (fork F-209-1); -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) the value of the transaction is not greater, and its terms are not more favourable, than it is reasonable to expect the company would have offered to a person of the same financial standing but unconnected with the company"

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 210 Other relevant transactions or arrangements
-- ======================================================================================================================

DECLARE `s 210 the person for whom the transaction in question is entered into` IS ONE OF
    `s 210(3)(a) a director of the company entering into it`
    `s 210(3)(b) a person connected with a director of the company entering into it`
    `s 210(4)(a) a director of the holding company of the company entering into it`
    `s 210(4)(b) a person connected with a director of the holding company of the company entering into it`
    `s 210 someone else`

DECLARE `s 210 who entered into the other transaction or arrangement` IS ONE OF
    `s 210 the company entering into the transaction in question`
    `s 210 a subsidiary of the company entering into the transaction in question`
    `s 210 the holding company of the company entering into the transaction in question`
    `s 210 a subsidiary of the holding company`
    `s 210 someone else`

-- src:2765 | (3) Where the transaction or arrangement in question is entered into—
-- src:2766 | (a) for a director of the company entering into it, or
-- src:2767 | (b) for a person connected with such a director,
-- src:2768 | the conditions are that the transaction or arrangement was (or is) entered into for that director, or a person connected with him, by virtue of the relevant exception by that company or by any of its subsidiaries.
@ref s 210(3) the conditions where the transaction in question is for a director of the company or a connected person (src:2765-2768)
GIVEN `for whom the transaction in question is entered into` IS A `s 210 the person for whom the transaction in question is entered into`
      `the other transaction was entered into for that director, or a person connected with him, by virtue of the relevant exception` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by whom` IS A `s 210 who entered into the other transaction or arrangement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 210(3) the conditions are met` MEANS
    CONSIDER `for whom the transaction in question is entered into`
    WHEN `s 210(3)(a) a director of the company entering into it` THEN `s 210(3) the conditions test`
    WHEN `s 210(3)(b) a person connected with a director of the company entering into it` THEN `s 210(3) the conditions test`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the transaction or arrangement in question is entered into— (a) for a director of the company entering into it, or (b) for a person connected with such a director"
    WHERE
        `s 210(3) the conditions test` MEANS
            IF `the other transaction was entered into for that director, or a person connected with him, by virtue of the relevant exception`
               AND (   `by whom` EQUALS `s 210 the company entering into the transaction in question`
                    OR `by whom` EQUALS `s 210 a subsidiary of the company entering into the transaction in question`)
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the conditions are that the transaction or arrangement was (or is) entered into for that director, or a person connected with him, by virtue of the relevant exception by that company or by any of its subsidiaries"

-- src:2769 | (4) Where the transaction or arrangement in question is entered into—
-- src:2770 | (a) for a director of the holding company of the company entering into it, or
-- src:2771 | (b) for a person connected with such a director,
-- src:2772 | the conditions are that the transaction or arrangement was (or is) entered into for that director, or a person connected with him, by virtue of the relevant exception by the holding company or by any of its subsidiaries.
@ref s 210(4) the conditions where the transaction in question is for a director of the holding company or a connected person (src:2769-2772)
GIVEN `for whom the transaction in question is entered into` IS A `s 210 the person for whom the transaction in question is entered into`
      `the other transaction was entered into for that director, or a person connected with him, by virtue of the relevant exception` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by whom` IS A `s 210 who entered into the other transaction or arrangement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 210(4) the conditions are met` MEANS
    CONSIDER `for whom the transaction in question is entered into`
    WHEN `s 210(4)(a) a director of the holding company of the company entering into it` THEN `s 210(4) the conditions test`
    WHEN `s 210(4)(b) a person connected with a director of the holding company of the company entering into it` THEN `s 210(4) the conditions test`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the transaction or arrangement in question is entered into— (a) for a director of the holding company of the company entering into it, or (b) for a person connected with such a director"
    WHERE
        `s 210(4) the conditions test` MEANS
            IF `the other transaction was entered into for that director, or a person connected with him, by virtue of the relevant exception`
               AND (   `by whom` EQUALS `s 210 the holding company of the company entering into the transaction in question`
                    OR `by whom` EQUALS `s 210 a subsidiary of the holding company`)
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the conditions are that the transaction or arrangement was (or is) entered into for that director, or a person connected with him, by virtue of the relevant exception by the holding company or by any of its subsidiaries"

-- src:2773 | (5) A transaction or arrangement entered into by a company that at the time it was entered into—
-- src:2774 | (a) was a subsidiary of the company entering into the transaction or arrangement in question, or
-- src:2775 | (b) was a subsidiary of that company's holding company,
-- src:2776 | is not a relevant transaction or arrangement if, at the time the question arises whether the transaction or arrangement in question falls within a relevant exception, it is no longer such a subsidiary.
@ref s 210(5) a former subsidiary's transaction (src:2773-2776)
GIVEN `at the time it was entered into the other transaction's maker was a subsidiary of the company entering into the transaction in question, or of that company's holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time the question arises the maker is still such a subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 210(5) the transaction or arrangement is not a relevant transaction or arrangement` MEANS
    IF `at the time it was entered into the other transaction's maker was a subsidiary of the company entering into the transaction in question, or of that company's holding company`
       AND (NOT `at the time the question arises the maker is still such a subsidiary`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not a relevant transaction or arrangement if, at the time the question arises ..., it is no longer such a subsidiary" (this subsection does not exclude it on these facts; it says nothing of whether the transaction is relevant)

-- src:2764 | (2) Other relevant transactions or arrangements are those previously entered into, or entered into at the same time as the transaction or arrangement in question in relation to which the following conditions are met.
@ref s 210(2) other relevant transactions or arrangements (src:2764-2764)
GIVEN `previously entered into, or entered into at the same time as the transaction in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 210(3) the conditions are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 210(4) the conditions are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 210(5) the transaction or arrangement is not a relevant transaction or arrangement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 210(2) the other transaction or arrangement is a relevant transaction or arrangement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `previously entered into, or entered into at the same time as the transaction in question`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Other relevant transactions or arrangements are those previously entered into, or entered into at the same time as the transaction or arrangement in question in relation to which the following conditions are met"
        IF `s 210(5) the transaction or arrangement is not a relevant transaction or arrangement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not a relevant transaction or arrangement if, at the time the question arises ..., it is no longer such a subsidiary"
        IF `s 210(3) the conditions are met` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 210(4) the conditions are met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 210(3) the conditions are met` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `s 210(4) the conditions are met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to which the following conditions are met" (the conditions of (3) and of (4) are both stated and neither is met)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): (3) and (4) each speak only where the transaction in question is entered into for a director (or connected person) of the company or of its holding company; with only one of them engaged and unmet, or an answer unknown, the text does not decide

-- "The relevant exception" (second paragraph of subsection (1)) is the exception for the purposes of which the question arises:
-- it is the fact `by virtue of the relevant exception` that s 210(3) and (4) take as an input.
-- src:2761 | 210 Other relevant transactions or arrangements
-- src:2762 | (1) This section has effect for determining what are “other relevant transactions or arrangements” for the purposes of any exception to section 197, 198, 200 or 201.
-- src:2763 | In the following provisions “the relevant exception” means the exception for the purposes of which that falls to be determined.
@ref s 210(1) the section's scope (src:2761-2763)
GIVEN `the provision is an exception to section 197, 198, 200 or 201` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 210(1) this section has effect for determining the other relevant transactions or arrangements` MEANS
    IF `the provision is an exception to section 197, 198, 200 or 201`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purposes of any exception to section 197, 198, 200 or 201"

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 211 The value of transactions and arrangements
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- src:2781 | (2) The value of a loan is the amount of its principal.
@ref s 211(2) the value of a loan (src:2781)
GIVEN principal IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 211(2) the value of a loan` MEANS principal

-- src:2782 | (3) The value of a quasi-loan is the amount, or maximum amount, that the person to whom the quasi-loan is made is liable to reimburse the creditor.
@ref s 211(3) the value of a quasi-loan (src:2782)
GIVEN `the amount, or maximum amount, the person to whom the quasi-loan is made is liable to reimburse the creditor` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 211(3) the value of a quasi-loan` MEANS `the amount, or maximum amount, the person to whom the quasi-loan is made is liable to reimburse the creditor`

-- src:2783 | (4) The value of a credit transaction is the price that it is reasonable to expect could be obtained for the goods, services or land to which the transaction relates if they had been supplied (at the time the transaction is entered into) in the ordinary course of business and on the same terms (apart from price) as they have been supplied, or are to be supplied, under the transaction in question.
@ref s 211(4) the value of a credit transaction (src:2783)
GIVEN `the price it is reasonable to expect could be obtained for the goods, services or land had they been supplied at the time in the ordinary course of business on the same terms (apart from price)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 211(4) the value of a credit transaction` MEANS `the price it is reasonable to expect could be obtained for the goods, services or land had they been supplied at the time in the ordinary course of business on the same terms (apart from price)`

-- src:2784 | (5) The value of a guarantee or security is the amount guaranteed or secured.
@ref s 211(5) the value of a guarantee or security (src:2784)
GIVEN `the amount guaranteed or secured` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 211(5) the value of a guarantee or security` MEANS `the amount guaranteed or secured`

-- src:2785 | (6) The value of an arrangement to which section 203 (related arrangements) applies is the value of the transaction to which the arrangement relates.
@ref s 211(6) the value of a related arrangement (src:2785)
GIVEN `the value of the transaction to which the arrangement relates` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 211(6) the value of an arrangement to which section 203 applies` MEANS `the value of the transaction to which the arrangement relates`

DECLARE `s 211 transaction or arrangement` IS ONE OF
    `s 211(2) a loan` HAS `s 211(2) principal` IS A NUMBER
    `s 211(3) a quasi-loan` HAS `s 211(3) amount or maximum amount to be reimbursed` IS A NUMBER
    `s 211(4) a credit transaction` HAS `s 211(4) reasonable price` IS A NUMBER
    `s 211(5) a guarantee or security` HAS `s 211(5) amount guaranteed or secured` IS A NUMBER
    `s 211(6) an arrangement to which section 203 applies` HAS `s 211(6) value of the related transaction` IS A NUMBER

-- src:2778 | (1) For the purposes of sections 197 to 214 (loans etc)—
-- src:2779 | (a) the value of a transaction or arrangement is determined as follows, and
-- src:2780 | (b) the value of any other relevant transaction or arrangement is taken to be the value so determined reduced by any amount by which the liabilities of the person for whom the transaction or arrangement was made have been reduced.
@ref s 211(1)(a) value determined as follows (src:2778-2780)
GIVEN transaction IS A `s 211 transaction or arrangement`
      `its value is capable of being expressed as a specific sum of money` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 211 value`
`s 211(1)(a) the value of the transaction or arrangement` MEANS
    IF `its value is capable of being expressed as a specific sum of money`
    THEN `s 211 a specific sum` `the specific sum`
    ELSE `s 211 deemed to exceed 50000 pounds` -- s 211(7)
    WHERE
        `the specific sum` MEANS
            CONSIDER transaction
            WHEN `s 211(2) a loan` p THEN `s 211(2) the value of a loan` p
            WHEN `s 211(3) a quasi-loan` p THEN `s 211(3) the value of a quasi-loan` p
            WHEN `s 211(4) a credit transaction` p THEN `s 211(4) the value of a credit transaction` p
            WHEN `s 211(5) a guarantee or security` p THEN `s 211(5) the value of a guarantee or security` p
            WHEN `s 211(6) an arrangement to which section 203 applies` p THEN `s 211(6) the value of an arrangement to which section 203 applies` p

-- src:2786 | (7) If the value of a transaction or arrangement is not capable of being expressed as a specific sum of money—
-- src:2787 | (a) whether because the amount of any liability arising under the transaction or arrangement is unascertainable, or for any other reason, and
-- src:2788 | (b) whether or not any liability under the transaction or arrangement has been reduced,
-- src:2789 | its value is deemed to exceed £50,000.
@ref s 211(7) value not capable of being expressed as a specific sum (src:2786-2789)
GIVEN `its value is capable of being expressed as a specific sum of money` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 211(7) the value is deemed to exceed 50,000 pounds` MEANS
    IF `its value is capable of being expressed as a specific sum of money`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the value of a transaction or arrangement is not capable of being expressed as a specific sum of money ... its value is deemed to exceed £50,000" (the deeming does not apply to a value that can be so expressed)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- The value of any OTHER relevant transaction or arrangement: the value so determined, reduced by any amount by which the liabilities
-- of the person for whom it was made have been reduced. The text does not say the result cannot fall below nought (fork F-211-1).
-- src:2780 | (b) the value of any other relevant transaction or arrangement is taken to be the value so determined reduced by any amount by which the liabilities of the person for whom the transaction or arrangement was made have been reduced.
@ref s 211(1)(b) the value of other relevant transactions (src:2780-2780)
GIVEN `the value so determined` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount by which the liabilities of the person for whom the transaction or arrangement was made have been reduced` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 211(1)(b) the value of an other relevant transaction or arrangement` MEANS
    `the value so determined` MINUS `the amount by which the liabilities of the person for whom the transaction or arrangement was made have been reduced`

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 212 The person for whom a transaction or arrangement is entered into
-- ======================================================================================================================

DECLARE `s 212 transaction or arrangement` IS ONE OF
    `s 212(a) a loan or quasi-loan` HAS `s 212(a) person to whom it is made` IS A STRING
    `s 212(b) a credit transaction` HAS `s 212(b) person to whom goods, land or services are supplied, sold, hired, leased or otherwise disposed of` IS A STRING
    `s 212(c) a guarantee or security` HAS `s 212(c) person for whom the transaction is made in connection with which it is entered into` IS A STRING
    `s 212(d) an arrangement within section 203` HAS `s 212(d) person for whom the transaction is made to which the arrangement relates` IS A STRING

-- src:2790 | 212 The person for whom a transaction or arrangement is entered into
-- src:2791 | For the purposes of sections 197 to 214 (loans etc) the person for whom a transaction or arrangement is entered into is—
-- src:2792 | (a) in the case of a loan or quasi-loan, the person to whom it is made;
-- src:2793 | (b) in the case of a credit transaction, the person to whom goods, land or services are supplied, sold, hired, leased or otherwise disposed of under the transaction;
-- src:2794 | (c) in the case of a guarantee or security, the person for whom the transaction is made in connection with which the guarantee or security is entered into;
-- src:2795 | (d) in the case of an arrangement within section 203 (related arrangements), the person for whom the transaction is made to which the arrangement relates.
@ref s 212 the person for whom a transaction or arrangement is entered into (src:2790-2795)
GIVEN transaction IS A `s 212 transaction or arrangement`
GIVETH A STRING
`s 212 the person for whom the transaction or arrangement is entered into` MEANS
    CONSIDER transaction
    WHEN `s 212(a) a loan or quasi-loan` p THEN p
    WHEN `s 212(b) a credit transaction` p THEN p
    WHEN `s 212(c) a guarantee or security` p THEN p
    WHEN `s 212(d) an arrangement within section 203` p THEN p

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 213 Loans etc: civil consequences of contravention
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- The five requirements are coa4's (ss 197, 198, 200, 201, 203); each input is that part's answer to "was the requirement contravened".
-- src:2797 | (1) This section applies where a company enters into a transaction or arrangement in contravention of section 197, 198, 200, 201 or 203 (requirement of members' approval for loans etc).
@ref s 213(1) application of the section (src:2797-2797)
GIVEN `s 197 the transaction or arrangement was entered into in contravention of section 197` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 198 the transaction or arrangement was entered into in contravention of section 198` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 200 the transaction or arrangement was entered into in contravention of section 200` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 201 the transaction or arrangement was entered into in contravention of section 201` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 203 the transaction or arrangement was entered into in contravention of section 203` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 213(1) this section applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF    `s 197 the transaction or arrangement was entered into in contravention of section 197` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `s 198 the transaction or arrangement was entered into in contravention of section 198` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `s 200 the transaction or arrangement was entered into in contravention of section 200` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `s 201 the transaction or arrangement was entered into in contravention of section 201` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `s 203 the transaction or arrangement was entered into in contravention of section 203` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF    `s 197 the transaction or arrangement was entered into in contravention of section 197` EQUALS JUST FALSE
           AND `s 198 the transaction or arrangement was entered into in contravention of section 198` EQUALS JUST FALSE
           AND `s 200 the transaction or arrangement was entered into in contravention of section 200` EQUALS JUST FALSE
           AND `s 201 the transaction or arrangement was entered into in contravention of section 201` EQUALS JUST FALSE
           AND `s 203 the transaction or arrangement was entered into in contravention of section 203` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where a company enters into a transaction or arrangement in contravention of section 197, 198, 200, 201 or 203"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether a requirement of ss 197 to 203 was contravened is coa4's answer and at least one answer is unknown

-- src:2798 | (2) The transaction or arrangement is voidable at the instance of the company, unless—
-- src:2799 | (a) restitution of any money or other asset that was the subject matter of the transaction or arrangement is no longer possible,
-- src:2800 | (b) the company has been indemnified for any loss or damage resulting from the transaction or arrangement, or
-- src:2801 | (c) rights acquired in good faith, for value and without actual notice of the contravention by a person who is not a party to the transaction or arrangement would be affected by the avoidance.
@ref s 213(2) voidable at the instance of the company (src:2798-2801)
GIVEN `s 213(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `restitution of any money or other asset that was the subject matter is no longer possible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has been indemnified for any loss or damage resulting from the transaction or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `rights acquired in good faith, for value and without actual notice of the contravention by a person who is not a party would be affected by the avoidance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 213(2) the transaction or arrangement is voidable at the instance of the company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 213(1) this section applies`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 213(1) depends on the answers of ss 197 to 203 (coa4)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies where" (this section says nothing of a transaction outside it)
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
         IF    `restitution of any money or other asset that was the subject matter is no longer possible`
            OR `the company has been indemnified for any loss or damage resulting from the transaction or arrangement`
            OR `rights acquired in good faith, for value and without actual notice of the contravention by a person who is not a party would be affected by the avoidance`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is voidable at the instance of the company, unless— (a) restitution ... is no longer possible, (b) the company has been indemnified ..., or (c) rights acquired in good faith"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 213(4) the person's position` IS ONE OF
    `s 213(4)(a) a director of the company or of its holding company with whom the company entered into the transaction or arrangement`
    `s 213(4)(b) a person with whom the company entered into the transaction or arrangement who is connected with a director of the company or of its holding company`
    `s 213(4)(c) the director of the company or of its holding company with whom any such person is connected`
    `s 213(4)(d) any other director of the company who authorised the transaction or arrangement`
    `s 213(4) none of these`

DECLARE `s 213 section contravened` IS ONE OF
    `s 213 section 197`
    `s 213 section 198`
    `s 213 section 200`
    `s 213 section 201`
    `s 213 section 203`

-- src:2805 | (4) The persons so liable are—
-- src:2806 | (a) any director of the company or of its holding company with whom the company entered into the transaction or arrangement in contravention of section 197, 198, 201 or 203,
-- src:2807 | (b) any person with whom the company entered into the transaction or arrangement in contravention of any of those sections who is connected with a director of the company or of its holding company,
-- src:2808 | (c) the director of the company or of its holding company with whom any such person is connected, and
-- src:2809 | (d) any other director of the company who authorised the transaction or arrangement.
@ref s 213(4) the persons liable (src:2805-2809)
GIVEN position IS A `s 213(4) the person's position`
      contravened IS A `s 213 section contravened`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 213(4) the person is one of the persons liable` MEANS
    CONSIDER position
    WHEN `s 213(4) none of these` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The persons so liable are— (a) ... (b) ... (c) ... (d) ..." (no "only")
    WHEN `s 213(4)(d) any other director of the company who authorised the transaction or arrangement` THEN JUST TRUE -- (d) names no section: any contravention of s 197, 198, 200, 201 or 203
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER contravened
        WHEN `s 213 section 200` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): (a) and (b) name "section 197, 198, 201 or 203" and (b), (c) say "any of those sections"; s 200 is not among them (fork F-213-1)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:2811 | (6) In the case of a transaction or arrangement entered into by a company in contravention of section 200, 201 or 203 with a person connected with a director of the company or of its holding company, that director is not liable by virtue of subsection (4)(c) if he shows that he took all reasonable steps to secure the company's compliance with the section concerned.
@ref s 213(6) a director whose connected person contravened (src:2811-2811)
GIVEN position IS A `s 213(4) the person's position`
      contravened IS A `s 213 section contravened`
      `the transaction was with a person connected with a director of the company or of its holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he shows that he took all reasonable steps to secure the company's compliance with the section concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 213(6) the director is not liable by virtue of subsection (4)(c)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF position EQUALS `s 213(4)(c) the director of the company or of its holding company with whom any such person is connected`
           AND (contravened EQUALS `s 213 section 200` OR contravened EQUALS `s 213 section 201` OR contravened EQUALS `s 213 section 203`)
           AND `the transaction was with a person connected with a director of the company or of its holding company`
           AND `he shows that he took all reasonable steps to secure the company's compliance with the section concerned`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF position EQUALS `s 213(4)(c) the director of the company or of its holding company with whom any such person is connected`
           AND (contravened EQUALS `s 213 section 200` OR contravened EQUALS `s 213 section 201` OR contravened EQUALS `s 213 section 203`)
           AND `the transaction was with a person connected with a director of the company or of its holding company`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that director is not liable by virtue of subsection (4)(c) if he shows that he took all reasonable steps" (this subsection gives no defence on these facts)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a transaction or arrangement entered into by a company in contravention of section 200, 201 or 203 with a person connected with a director ..., that director is not liable by virtue of subsection (4)(c)"

-- src:2812 | (7) In any case—
-- src:2813 | (a) a person so connected is not liable by virtue of subsection (4)(b), and
-- src:2814 | (b) a director is not liable by virtue of subsection (4)(d),
-- src:2815 | if he shows that, at the time the transaction or arrangement was entered into, he did not know the relevant circumstances constituting the contravention.
@ref s 213(7) a connected person or a director who did not know (src:2812-2815)
GIVEN position IS A `s 213(4) the person's position`
      `he shows that, at the time the transaction or arrangement was entered into, he did not know the relevant circumstances constituting the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 213(7) the person is not liable by virtue of subsection (4)(b) or (d)` MEANS
    CONSIDER position
    WHEN `s 213(4)(b) a person with whom the company entered into the transaction or arrangement who is connected with a director of the company or of its holding company` THEN `s 213(7) the showing` -- (7)(a)
    WHEN `s 213(4)(d) any other director of the company who authorised the transaction or arrangement` THEN `s 213(7) the showing` -- (7)(b)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) a person so connected is not liable by virtue of subsection (4)(b), and (b) a director is not liable by virtue of subsection (4)(d)"
    WHERE
        `s 213(7) the showing` MEANS
            IF `he shows that, at the time the transaction or arrangement was entered into, he did not know the relevant circumstances constituting the contravention`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if he shows that, at the time the transaction or arrangement was entered into, he did not know the relevant circumstances constituting the contravention" (this subsection gives no defence on these facts)

-- src:2802 | (3) Whether or not the transaction or arrangement has been avoided, each of the persons specified in subsection (4) is liable—
-- src:2803 | (a) to account to the company for any gain that he has made directly or indirectly by the transaction or arrangement, and
-- src:2804 | (b) (jointly and severally with any other person so liable under this section) to indemnify the company for any loss or damage resulting from the transaction or arrangement.
@ref s 213(3) liability to account and to indemnify (src:2802-2804)
GIVEN `s 213(4) the person is one of the persons liable` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 213(6) the director is not liable by virtue of subsection (4)(c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 213(7) the person is not liable by virtue of subsection (4)(b) or (d)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 213(3) the person is liable to account to the company for any gain and to indemnify it for any loss` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 213(4) the person is one of the persons liable` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "each of the persons specified in subsection (4) is liable" says nothing of a person outside the list
        IF `s 213(6) the director is not liable by virtue of subsection (4)(c)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that director is not liable by virtue of subsection (4)(c) if he shows that he took all reasonable steps"
        IF `s 213(7) the person is not liable by virtue of subsection (4)(b) or (d)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person so connected is not liable by virtue of subsection (4)(b), and a director is not liable by virtue of subsection (4)(d), if he shows that, at the time ... he did not know"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE -- (3), subject to (6) and (7) ("Subsections (3) and (4) are subject to the following two subsections", subsection (5)): a defence that is not shown, or does not arise, leaves the liability

-- src:2810 | (5) Subsections (3) and (4) are subject to the following two subsections.
@ref s 213(5) subsections (3) and (4) are subject to subsections (6) and (7) (src:2810-2810)
GIVEN `the liability is under subsection (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 213(5) the liability is subject to subsections (6) and (7)` MEANS
    IF `the liability is under subsection (3) or (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsections (3) and (4) are subject to the following two subsections"

-- (3)(a): "to account to the company for any gain that he has made directly or indirectly by the transaction or arrangement".
-- src:2803 | (a) to account to the company for any gain that he has made directly or indirectly by the transaction or arrangement, and
@ref s 213(3)(a) the amount to account for (src:2803-2803)
GIVEN liable IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, `the gain he has made directly or indirectly by the transaction or arrangement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 213(3)(a) the amount the person must account to the company for` MEANS
    CONSIDER liable
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST `the gain he has made directly or indirectly by the transaction or arrangement`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST 0 -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not liable" (nothing is owed under this subsection)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether he is liable is not known

-- (3)(b): "(jointly and severally with any other person so liable under this section) to indemnify the company for any loss or damage":
-- each person liable is liable for the whole loss; the amount each can recover is a matter for the court (not covered).
-- src:2804 | (b) (jointly and severally with any other person so liable under this section) to indemnify the company for any loss or damage resulting from the transaction or arrangement.
@ref s 213(3)(b) the amount to indemnify the company for (src:2804-2804)
GIVEN liable IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, `the loss or damage resulting from the transaction or arrangement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 213(3)(b) the amount the person, jointly and severally with others liable, must indemnify the company for` MEANS
    CONSIDER liable
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST `the loss or damage resulting from the transaction or arrangement`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST 0 -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not liable" (nothing is owed under this subsection)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether he is liable is not known

-- src:2816 | (8) Nothing in this section shall be read as excluding the operation of any other enactment or rule of law by virtue of which the transaction or arrangement may be called in question or any liability to the company may arise.
@ref s 213(8) other enactments and rules of law are not excluded (src:2816-2816)
`s 213(8) this section excludes the operation of any other enactment or rule of law` MEANS
    JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section shall be read as excluding the operation of any other enactment or rule of law"

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 214 Loans etc: effect of subsequent affirmation
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- "Within a reasonable period" is a judgment the text leaves open: it is a plain input.
-- src:2818 | Where a transaction or arrangement is entered into by a company in contravention of section 197, 198, 200, 201 or 203 (requirement of members' approval for loans etc) but, within a reasonable period, it is affirmed—
-- src:2819 | (a) in the case of a contravention of the requirement for a resolution of the members of the company, by a resolution of the members of the company, and
-- src:2820 | (b) in the case of a contravention of the requirement for a resolution of the members of the company's holding company, by a resolution of the members of the holding company,
-- src:2821 | the transaction or arrangement may no longer be avoided under section 213.
@ref s 214 effect of subsequent affirmation (src:2818-2821)
GIVEN `s 213(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is affirmed within a reasonable period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contravention was of the requirement for a resolution of the members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is affirmed by a resolution of the members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contravention was of the requirement for a resolution of the members of the company's holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is affirmed by a resolution of the members of the holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 214 the transaction or arrangement may no longer be avoided under section 213` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 213(1) this section applies` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the transaction was entered into in contravention of ss 197 to 203 is coa4's answer and is not known
        IF `s 213(1) this section applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a transaction or arrangement is entered into by a company in contravention of section 197, 198, 200, 201 or 203"
        IF NOT `it is affirmed within a reasonable period`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but, within a reasonable period, it is affirmed"
        IF    (`the contravention was of the requirement for a resolution of the members of the company` OR `the contravention was of the requirement for a resolution of the members of the company's holding company`)
           AND ((NOT `the contravention was of the requirement for a resolution of the members of the company`) OR `it is affirmed by a resolution of the members of the company`)
           AND ((NOT `the contravention was of the requirement for a resolution of the members of the company's holding company`) OR `it is affirmed by a resolution of the members of the holding company`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) in the case of a contravention of the requirement for a resolution of the members of the company, by a resolution of the members of the company, and (b) ... of the holding company, by a resolution of the members of the holding company"
